{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why","id":1116926,"title":"Least Favorite Splat (and why)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-16T11:44:44-07:00","id":1116926,"title":"Least Favorite Splat (and why)","content":"I tried looking to see if anything similar had been posted and didn't see anything, so if this has already been discussed, I apologize. <br /> <br /> The only splats I've played are VtM, WtA, MtA and MtR, and Mummy only briefly, so I guess that doesn't count. Of the main three though, I dislike Werewolf the most. Here's why, best I can sum up:<ul><li>I dislike the &quot;eco-terrorist&quot; angle</li> <li>I dislike how it feels like it centers around combat (at least in my experience)</li> <li>I am not a fan of the cosmology/spiritual aspect of the splat</li> </ul>I suppose overall, I just don't like the flavor, as it's been presented to me over the years, and I started playing WoD in 1998. I freely admit it could have been my first ST who left the bad taste, but that colors one's experience. <br /> <br /> Anyway, what's your least favorite splat and why? I'm curious to see your answers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5128-synderryn","name":"Synderryn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T12:04:32-07:00","id":1116931,"title":"","content":"It would be easier to say the splats I do like, which would just be Wraith and Demon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T13:02:14-07:00","id":1116953,"title":"","content":"I dislike what Hunters are, altrough I like what they could be.<br /> <br /> They had so much potential in their corebook as empowered humans who are revealed what lies in the shadows, and then choose how to act about that...but in the following material most of this wasn't explored.<br /> Messengers are untrustworthy, they have their own agenda that includes giving most hunters a bias against monsters (monsters fell &quot;wrong&quot;), and the average hunter it's supposed to be OK with them. Add to that the fact that hunters go mystically insane as they improve their powers, and you don't seem to be <i>that </i>free to make your choice anymore.<br /> <br /> Most hunters seem to be decided to &quot;protect humanity&quot; and those who don't are a bunch of inocents that always end giving problems to supernaturals nevertheless (they always seem to guide a crazy hunter towards their supernatural contact). In the coreebok there was an evil hunter that wanted to control the dark powers for it's own interest, I liked that devilish idea to try to take or understand the power of the supernaturals, and use it, but this kind of aproaches were never given atention (even the Hunter who's possessed by an Earthbound wants the power just to get revenge from something monsters did).<br /> <br /> I feel that the themes of &quot;being scared in front of the supernatural&quot; and &quot;protecting humanity&quot; ended overshadowing every other theme that was present in the corebook.I want my hunters to be really divided about how to deal with the existence of the supernatural. I don't want my hunters to be always divided between the guy that messes with the supernatural in a careless fashion causing someone to take a shotgun and start a fight...and the guy with the shotgun...if you get what I'm saying...<br /> <br /> Also Hunter powers are so supernatural that you need to be really blind to think yourself a human (Oh, but we don't detect ourselves as supers!. Yeah, but everyone else's do...) <hr /><br /> I dislike Demon rules, if wasn't for that they could be one of my most favorite splats, but I REALLY dislike their rules.<br /> <br /> Demons wielding Static Magic (that work like Thaumaturgy/Disciplines)?. No, thank you.<br /> <br /> Pacts limited to give a few stat increases and perhaps a minor magic power that ends being weaker than being a Ghoul?, I prefer to have more leeway with my pacts, thank you.<br /> <br /> Also pacts as merely a way to feed are boring. Demons end being psychic vampires, I want pacts to be more than that (let them damn the soul if done cartelessly, let them be a way to go up in the infernal hiearachy, let them be a way to shape the world. Give me SOMETHING so I can believe Demons aren't just fancy vampires). Faustians are supposedly creating a net of Faith as a weapon to break the doors of Heaven, I need pacts to be more than free blood points to make <i>that </i>threatening.<br /> <br /> Also the demonic hierarchy it's boring. The only difference between a Duke and a lowly Fallen it's that the Duke starts with more points. Which doesn't seem to follow the Metaplot at all, as in the plot hierarchy does imply a hughe gap of potential. For one of the preffered ways to end Creation itself to be to release the most powerful Demons from Hell (that weren't able to make it trough the craks of hell 'cause they were too potent), I need the most powerful demons to be something more than a normal character with a lot of px","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-16-2017, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T16:30:46-07:00","id":1117006,"title":"","content":"Before C20, I generally would have gone with Changeling. It was for a very long time to me the weakest of the lines in terms of both getting its themes across, and actually being fun to play. The themes were muddled consistently by inconsistency, and the mechanics were too much work for the result. C20 has fixed a lot of that, though I guess I still have some lingering biases from the 20 years of unfun for it to move up much farther in my rankings. But it's certainly moved up from the bottom to be at least tied with:<br /> <br /> Vampire! Yep. Masquerade has consistently been one of my least favorite of the WoD games. For me, it's sort of the flip side of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> with Hunter. VtM explores too much without the flexibility to really do any of it justice. With most of the other games, I've always felt that the expansive nature of them was well complemented by easy to turn dials. VtM always feels like it's tripping over itself. It's about politics... but the politics are inconsequential to the Sect war, which isn't really political gaming. It's dark superheroes with fangs, but then the personal horror parts get in the way. It's personal horror, but everything that game presents you to do takes you away from that. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T20:49:58-07:00","id":1117073,"title":"","content":"Demons from DtF for a number of reasons. You are an alien invader from another level of reality whose purpose is to lead the way for a mass invasion of your kind so that humanity is enslaved. Oh, and they offered much worse deals to their followers than the other types of Demons in the oWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-17T14:40:09-07:00","id":1117444,"title":"","content":"To deal with, Mages. Can't stand the system, can't stand that it always ends in discussions how vulgar what action is and I could never get my mind around the functions of the spheres and the Umbra and the whole other things that make the setting cool to others but sucky for me. Maybe I'm just too dumb, but Mage never did it for me...<br /> <br /> To play, it's Wraith. And I have to be clear here, I love Wraith from a conceptional point, I like the fact that it's such a bleak and soul wrecking setting and I deeply respect what they creators were going for. But it plays really badly. And my players always go into depression once they notice that there is basically not a single place in our home where you don't run into dybbuks all the time. And that really darkens the mood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:54:45-07:00","id":1117777,"title":"","content":"Hunter was my least favorite, as the use of playable characters from other games as a monster manual bothered me.<br /> <br /> That said, I did like Hunter. I didn't really <i>hate</i> or even <i>dislike</i> any of the WoD games. The only one I never read, however, was Demon.<br /> <br /> I only ST'd Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, and Changeling. I've used elements of all five of the original games in my Mage game, and I've played everything but Demon and Mummy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T11:19:29-07:00","id":1117862,"title":"","content":"Reckoning is my least favorite, with Demon running a close second. I was expecting something more like Vigil. Instead we get people who delude themselves into thinking they're still human despite their powers. And go insane from having that power. Bad STing and worse roleplaying didn't help matters, with other PCs being targeted for existing. Demon feels like a ripoff of Changeling. I didn't mind the few Reconcilers we ran into, but every other faction tended to be pointlessly aggressive, which is not very much fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T13:47:51-07:00","id":1117918,"title":"","content":"Werewolf was my least favorite by far. I've been a fan of werewolf horror fiction since I was a teenager, and discarding most of its motifs and tropes in favor of a bunch of furry New Age ecoterrorists crusading against The Man... er, The Wyrm did not sit well with me. Black Fox's reimagination of the garou as essentially inhuman cultists worshiping a Lovecraftean fertility god is the only take on the game I've ever heard that sounded appealing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T14:21:01-07:00","id":1117928,"title":"","content":"Let's see.<br /> <br /> Least favorite: Wraith. I like the setting, it has much fun stuff, but I'd rather like to use it for a backdrop for the other games. I'm just disinterested in playing ghosts, because all the reasons it implies.<br /> <br /> Second least: Demon. I was okay with the level of &quot;yeah, Abrahamic religions got it right&quot; in Vampire, because it's really a myth there and nobody knows, but it's too much in Demon. Also, I just like &quot;demons&quot; as depicted in the other games more. I'm not saying the game doesn't have good parts, it has and the core concept is interesting, but overall I was never too motivated to play it, in comparison to the other ones. Also, like Aleph, I think it is too much like Vampire, in some aspects.<br /> <br /> Third: Hunter. For the same reasons the others wrote. I like Buffy, but I want a more Supernatural vibe in WoD, regarding hunters. I want mortals to fight back, with wits and tools, sheer determination and excellence, without the need and convenience to becoming another kind of supernatural. That concept is also okay, but I don't want it to be the most prevalent one. I want Hunter to be the game, which <i>isn't</i> about intrinsic superpowers. Vigil is maybe the one line I clearly preferred the NWoD version of, exactly because of those reasons.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I like the big three plus Changeling very much and the minor lines are okay/good too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T15:11:16-07:00","id":1117949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1117918#post1117918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> inhuman cultists worshiping a Lovecraftean fertility god is the only take on the game I've ever heard that sounded appealing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Saying it like that sounds pretty rad. I would play the heck out of it, but I don't like that it has Werewoves as a motif... <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T21:55:19-07:00","id":1118071,"title":"","content":"For me its probably still Demons. I just don't really get what their purpose was supposed to be. I find their aesthetic to be very edge-lord-y (and I say this as a Vampire fan), and I find their approach to lore, cosmology, and metaplot to somehow be even more condescending and douchey than Mages (which set a high bar).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T22:18:21-07:00","id":1118074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1118071#post1118071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me its probably still Demons. I just don't really get what their purpose was supposed to be. I find their aesthetic to be very edge-lord-y (and I say this as a Vampire fan), and I find their approach to lore, cosmology, and metaplot to somehow be even more condescending and douchey than Mages (which set a high bar).</div> </div> </div> </div>Agree, although I somewhat liked the book, aesthetic wise, but yeah, Vampire is better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T22:42:50-07:00","id":1118079,"title":"","content":"I honestly liked Mage till M20 came out, just way to many politics and not enough rules. I used to like a lot of the classic games but their Nwod/Chod replacements won me over. Then 2ed came out and the gender politics/social justice stuff kinda soured me on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T03:28:49-07:00","id":1118121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1118079#post1118079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then 2ed came out and the gender politics/social justice stuff kinda soured me on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair: If the writing was better, you wouldn't notice. But modern WW does like its ham fists","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13654-davesknd","name":"Davesknd","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"173"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T13:44:18-07:00","id":1118267,"title":"","content":"Wasn't <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13009_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13009\" data-vbnamecard=\"13009\">BurritoMage</a> meant the CofD 2eds?<br /> <br /> I still liked most of the 20th stuff, including M20 (and very much liked that one), but I'm not in favor how the writers of the various 20th books &quot;abandoned&quot; gothic-punk as an important part of the setting and every game. In older books, there was at least a few columns, designated to that and the 20ths don't even mention it, aside from the V20 core, and even that one did it only tangentially. It's just a big loss in my eyes, for a core theme and great descriptor of the whole setting to be ignored. I really hope Martin's remark of &quot;gothic-punk is dead&quot; doesn't mean it will be like that or even more so in V5 and in their iteration of WoD.<br /> <br /> But yeah, political correctness and inclusivity are very noticeable trends in the OPP books, and even more in the CofD ones. It's not surprising, regarding a lot of their writers and developers and honestly, most of the time isn't even a bad thing (although sometimes I feel it to be a bit forced). Ok, the WoD books were always leftist and attempted to be inclusive, but it's certainly a shift in focus and importance. Also, the old books were less PC in the sense that they were more &quot;dark&quot;, more &quot;edgy&quot;, but that was a good thing in my eyes. The new books are frequently a bit too... neat, IMO, albeit having tons of very good material and writing in them. I just liked the grittier version of WoD a bit better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 07-19-2017, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T13:57:22-07:00","id":1118271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1117006#post1117006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire! Yep. Masquerade has consistently been one of my least favorite of the WoD games. For me, it's sort of the flip side of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> with Hunter. VtM explores too much without the flexibility to really do any of it justice. With most of the other games, I've always felt that the expansive nature of them was well complemented by easy to turn dials. VtM always feels like it's tripping over itself. It's about politics... but the politics are inconsequential to the Sect war, which isn't really political gaming. It's dark superheroes with fangs, but then the personal horror parts get in the way. It's personal horror, but everything that game presents you to do takes you away from that. Etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, but honestly, not that surprising. I disagree, though. To me, one of the big merits of Vampire is it's inclusion of various themes and styles, from local politics to sect wars to uncovering ancient knowledge to personal horror and I always felt that the rules are flexible enough to support them, at least to an okay extent. I tend to regard games with very focused rules and themes on one thing to be less interesting on the long run (although they could be better in doing that particular thing, yes, absolutely). I guess that's why I generally like kitchen-sink fantasy and the kitchen-sink nature of WoD as a crossover setting too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 07-19-2017, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T14:31:06-07:00","id":1118278,"title":"","content":"I think you're misinterpreting me a bit there.<br /> <br /> I didn't say I have a problem with expansive games (Mage is only of my favorite WoD games and is by far the most thematically expansive). I said that I think VtM gets in its own way. Not just with the rules, but the nature of its setting elements.<br /> <br /> Like, with Mage, if I want to run a local politics Chantry game, the Ascension War part of the game easily compliments it even if there's never going to be a bunch of combat scenes with black helicopters and HITMarks, or space battles between blimps carrying magicwand fireball artillery vs. sci-fi space ships. The Ascension War can easily inform individual political stances on the local level, and picking a post-Revised point in the mtaplot, there's a lot of room for the Technocracy to impact the game directly without turning into a shooting war.<br /> <br /> Vampire has the Camarilla and Sabbat in active warfare the entire run, with the other Sects either taking a side or just hiding away. If I'm running a local politics oriented game, I need to set it far away from the Sect War. If the Sect War becomes a relevant part of the instance of the game, avoiding it turning into at least a side plot about violent conflict with other vampires is extremely convoluted. You can't just have some Sabbat take up residence in your Domain and make a deal for them to stay there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T14:49:00-07:00","id":1118286,"title":"","content":"I understand what you're getting into, but I never seen the sect war as that all-encompassing. It has its big battles and campaigns, like the Ascension War, with shoot-on-sight policies, regarding the other side in a given region, for a given time, but it has its casefires, infiltration, espionage, even &quot;deal with the devil&quot; situations too, again, just like the Ascension War. I mean, even Theo Bell, in the Brujah trilogy, worked with the Sabbat, to root out some nasty Nephandi. Guide to the Anarchs speaks about how the Anarchs have a relationship with the average Sabbat with a bit more leeway and could act as intermediaries.<br /> <br /> I think you could also do local politics just fine, without placing the story in a city far from the sect war, you just don't make it an open siege. Also, I think you could do personal horror without going into dark superheroes and vica versa. <br /> <br /> Also, it's not like the Ascension War was a less heated conflict, it's just, under the revised era, everyone had better things to do, to rebuild, than going for each other's throats with all their force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T16:17:39-07:00","id":1118300,"title":"","content":"Surprisingly for a WtA fan, the Changing Breeds never sat right with me. Mostly, because they were all different with different mechanics to the garou. Plus for example the bastet tribes compared to the garou ones seemed to put the felines in a very stereotyped position compared to the wolves. Or that Kitsune were solely asian, despite the myth of the clever fox being very common around the world. Having an unified ruleset how each shifter worked, and then having ones like ratkin just be another type of creature entirely.<br /> <br /> Generally, I think the CoD mentality of not tying everything to cosmologies and just letting there be weird outliers would have helped oWoD.<br /> <br /> Hunter is another one, the setting had great Hunter organizations all ready to use. The Imbued are neat, but kinda overshadow the older hunter orgs.<br /> <br /> Wraith, I generally like ghosts to be very simple creatures, complicating the matters isn't my style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T17:04:36-07:00","id":1118314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1118286#post1118286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand what you're getting into, but I never seen the sect war as that all-encompassing.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK so... you have a different opinion/experience than me. Care to disagree with everyone else too, or how about play Devil's Advocate even if you agree with them? Or just feeling like coming after me here because I opted to stop arguing with you in a different thread?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ..infiltration, espionage,... </div> </div> </div>Which is an entirely different mode of play that pulls things away from local politics focused play.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...in the Brujah trilogy... </div> </div> </div>And the novels are not considered part of the official metaplot/events/etc. unless one of the TT games includes it. The novels contradict the books in enough places I really don't care what's in them when it comes to how I view the actual games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you could also do local politics just fine, without placing the story in a city far from the sect war, you just don't make it an open siege. </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that pretty much all of North America east of the Rockies is &quot;open siege,&quot; west of the Rockies is dominated by the Anarch Free States, and... moving to South America, Africa, the Middle East, or most of Europe is pretty much exactly placing the story in a city far from the Sect War.<br /> <br /> Maybe this is just a difference of experience. Most people tend to play games set near where they live. In the official setting, every major (500K people or higher) city anywhere near me is part of the Sect War in the books. Yeah, I can ignore the books, I have plenty of times, but that's not a reason to make me like the game more. Las time I checked you don't live in a place where WW didn't detail out the ass to have to deal with or toss out to play the game you want to play; or set it somewhere far away and hope you're doing that place justice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it's not like the Ascension War was a less heated conflict, it's just, under the revised era, everyone had better things to do, to rebuild, than going for each other's throats with all their force. </div> </div> </div>I've played plenty of Mage 2e games that ignored the Ascension War, because mages are rare enough, and the setting vast enough, that there's lots to do. As well, the Ascension War is both global and nowhere. It's an ideological conflict not a territorial conflict like the Sect War is. The Traditions and Technocracy aren't fighting over control of cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T18:07:24-07:00","id":1118328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1118314#post1118314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK so... you have a different opinion/experience than me. Care to disagree with everyone else too, or how about play Devil's Advocate even if you agree with them? Or just feeling like coming after me here because I opted to stop arguing with you in a different thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Entirely disconnected from the other thread. The others here, I agreed with, or theirs were simple disliking of the themes of the given games. You gave specific reasons, regarding specific setting elements and concepts going in each others' and specific playstyles' way as a reason of your disliking and I find it worth to discuss. If you'd have said you dislike Vampire, for example, because you found its gothic aesthetic pretentious, or don't like the Christian background story, or the sects itself, or anything like that, just pure preference, or taste, I'd have said nothing, because there's nothing to argue about tastes.<br /> <br /> For example, the environmentalist angle is very important to my liking of Werewolf, but others hated it, as a theme and concept. Aside from stating the fact that it's actually one of the best parts of it to me (which I did in another topic recently too and I didn't feel repeating it here), I don't see here much to discuss.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is an entirely different mode of play that pulls things away from local politics focused play. </div> </div> </div>Depends. an infiltrator could absolutely be an important figure in local politics. Arguably, yes, I concede, you can't really have a sizeable and open representation of Cam and Sabbat in the same town, without some level of violent conflict, the way you could do in Requiem, or in Werewolf, with the Fera, or with the Traditions and Technocracy post-Avatar Storm, but I don't see those things as that much further apart. Thing is, factions in WoD are just quite warlike and antagonistic toward each other, it's a feature of the setting, I don't hink Vampire is quite spectacular here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the novels are not considered part of the official metaplot/events/etc. unless one of the TT games includes it. The novels contradict the books in enough places I really don't care what's in them when it comes to how I view the actual games. </div> </div> </div>Like the Clan Novel Saga? Or the Year of the Scarab? We could just agree to disagree, I tend to see fiction in WoD (and other rpgs) as a part of the whole narrative, not something entirely disconnected.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Keep in mind that pretty much all of North America east of the Rockies is &quot;open siege,&quot; west of the Rockies is dominated by the Anarch Free States, and... moving to South America, Africa, the Middle East, or most of Europe is pretty much exactly placing the story in a city far from the Sect War. </div> </div> </div>I don't think every city is open siege. Even the war on the east Coast was fairly short. As I recall, the New York By Night supplement didn't really described an active war zone, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe this is just a difference of experience. Most people tend to play games set near where they live. In the official setting, every major (500K people or higher) city anywhere near me is part of the Sect War in the books. Yeah, I can ignore the books, I have plenty of times, but that's not a reason to make me like the game more. Las time I checked you don't live in a place where WW didn't detail out the ass to have to deal with or toss out to play the game you want to play; or set it somewhere far away and hope you're doing that place justice. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it might be a differing experience. Although, I read probably the same books as you and I didn't get the picture that the majority of the US is open siege. On the contrary, I recall that most of Camarilla kindred are thinking about the Sabbat as a boogeyman, something isn't really real the elders are using to keep them in line. Yes there are active war zones and yes there were bigger campaigns in the metaplot but I just don't see it as an all-encompassing thing, regarding the big picture, something that involves every major city all the time and makes a local politics game unviable. I'm opt to, again, agree to disagree on it with you. Maybe we're both looking at the opposite extremes and the truth is somewhere in the middle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've played plenty of Mage 2e games that ignored the Ascension War, because mages are rare enough, and the setting vast enough, that there's lots to do. </div> </div> </div>As in Vampire, although I'm inclined to agreeing that Mage has <i>more </i>things to do, with all the Umbra, spirits and highly differing Traditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As well, the Ascension War is both global and nowhere. It's an ideological conflict not a territorial conflict like the Sect War is. The Traditions and Technocracy aren't fighting over control of cities. </div> </div> </div>Locally, I think the active Pogrom was quite like attempts to capture/kill/driving out mages from a given city. Yes, it wasn't a conflict about geographical dominions, as the sect war was, on the big picture, I agree, but for the mages of a given city, it probably was mostly the local Chantries vs. the local Technocracy.<br /> <br /> I don't want to convince you to like the game, it's your choice. You just stated your reason of dislike as something I thought of as worth discussing. Again, we could agree to disagree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 07-19-2017, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T18:19:00-07:00","id":1118331,"title":"","content":"I've enjoyed <i>reading</i> all of the WoD's game lines.<br /> <br /> But Demon, Hunter, and Changeling have been the only ones I didn't feel fired up at the prospect of running my own game for. The NWoD's versions are a lot more to my liking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T19:22:47-07:00","id":1118350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1118328#post1118328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You gave specific reasons, regarding specific setting elements and concepts going in each others' and specific playstyles' way as a reason of your disliking and I find it worth to discuss.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to discuss, we can discuss.<br /> <br /> Just disagreeing with lots of words isn't discussing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T20:51:01-07:00","id":1118396,"title":"","content":"Why, we wrote some arguments and counter-arguments back and forth. I provided examples backing up my argument and elaborated my opinion, while you elaborated on your part too. I conceded on some of your points and stated that nevertheless, I don't see it as dramatically as you, but that's okay, we don't have to see it the same way.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I'd call that a discussion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But anyway, it's not the thread about the importance and prevalence of sect wars in Vampire, so, if you're interested, one of us could make another thread on the Vampire forum about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 07-20-2017, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T01:04:50-07:00","id":1118435,"title":"","content":"Probably werewolf, because they never feel like werewolves. They are more like multi-classed D&amp;D Druid/Barbarians, and progression is more like deciding whether you'd like to be an Epic Barbarian with several Druid levels, or an Epic Druid with several Barbarian levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T03:25:24-07:00","id":1118465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1118435#post1118435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably werewolf, because they never feel like werewolves. They are more like multi-classed D&amp;D Druid/Barbarians, and progression is more like deciding whether you'd like to be an Epic Barbarian with several Druid levels, or an Epic Druid with several Barbarian levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually why I don't consider the garou true werewolves. They are too much like their very own race, rather than a cursed/infected person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T03:31:06-07:00","id":1118468,"title":"","content":"A lot of people have that problem with Werewolf, and I think it's understandable. WoD take on them was very unconventional when compared to, say, vampires.<br /> <br /> That reminds me of when I heard about Mage for the first time, before reading almost all the books. I was already into Vampire, I had played Ars Magica once, and I was aware of D&amp;D thanks to videogames, and into the pop culture fantasy sphere. When I heard about Mage this was my reaction:<br /> <br /> <i>But this isn't a game about wizards!, This is a game about hippies with reality warping powers!!!</i><br /> <br /> I like it now, I love it's freedom and amplitude, and I ended realizing that Mage's characters have more to do with real life mysticism than pop culture wizards, but it was my least favorite splat back then.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T13:55:01-07:00","id":1118692,"title":"","content":"Yeah, VtM actually does a better job of employing the tropes of infection, being cursed in a way that endangers everyone you love, and the inner struggle between man and beast that attract me to that sub-genre. In Werewolf you're born with a special destiny and the potential for kewl powerz rather than being cursed, you mostly associate with a pack of fellow furry superheroes who face minimal danger from your own transformations, and while technically man vs. beast is still a possible theme I've never observed anyone actually play out negative consequences arising from being an explosively violent rage monster in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T14:46:31-07:00","id":1118710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1118468#post1118468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of people have that problem with Werewolf, and I think it's understandable. WoD take on them was very unconventional when compared to, say, vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though, it's based on shapechanger myths, just not the traditional European Werewolf stories, so yeah, it was weird to me too, but in a good way. It was <i>different</i> form all the other werewolves in pop-culture and other rpgs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1118692#post1118692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, VtM actually does a better job of employing the tropes of infection, being cursed in a way that endangers everyone you love, and the inner struggle between man and beast that attract me to that sub-genre. In Werewolf you're born with a special destiny and the potential for kewl powerz rather than being cursed, you mostly associate with a pack of fellow furry superheroes who face minimal danger from your own transformations, and while technically man vs. beast is still a possible theme I've never observed anyone actually play out negative consequences arising from being an explosively violent rage monster in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, IMO. VtM jsut covered waaay too much of the man vs. beast and infection themes too extensively for a traditional werewolf game not to be too similar. Usually, in pop-culture, werewolves are the beasts, the savages and vampires are the lords, the cool, detached nobility of the night (and usually don't have the Beast as strong as a theme, if at all, jsut bloodlust. The struggle with the inner beast is a werewolf theme, mostly.), that's why the usual urban fantasy stuff could work, but VtM had the Gangrel and the Brujah and all those things, so how traditional werewolves could have been different enough to justify it?<br /> <br /> That said, I do miss traditional werevolves from WoD. Credit where credit's due, NWoD did some very nice things and the &quot;Skinchangers&quot; book was among them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1118468#post1118468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me of when I heard about Mage for the first time, before reading almost all the books. I was already into Vampire, I had played Ars Magica once, and I was aware of D&amp;D thanks to videogames, and into the pop culture fantasy sphere. When I heard about Mage this was my reaction:<br /> <br /> When I heard about Mage this was my reaction:<br /> <br /> <i>But this isn't a game about wizards!, This is a game about hippies with reality warping powers!!!</i><br /> <br /> I like it now, I love it's freedom and amplitude, and I ended realizing that Mage's characters have more to do with real life mysticism than pop culture wizards, but it was my least favorite splat back then.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What did you think about the Hermetics?<br /> <br /> Also, honestly, I think Mages are more sorcerers, than wizards. Funnily, Sorcerers are more like D&amp;D wizards, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 07-20-2017, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T16:27:04-07:00","id":1118751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1118692#post1118692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, VtM actually does a better job of employing the tropes of infection, being cursed in a way that endangers everyone you love, and the inner struggle between man and beast that attract me to that sub-genre. In Werewolf you're born with a special destiny and the potential for kewl powerz rather than being cursed, you mostly associate with a pack of fellow furry superheroes who face minimal danger from your own transformations, and while technically man vs. beast is still a possible theme I've never observed anyone actually play out negative consequences arising from being an explosively violent rage monster in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you are cursed, just not to have to chain yourself to a sturdy and immobile fixture in the basement every three days out of 28 or so. Aside from the transparently named Curse induced from Rage that makes it difficult to talk to anyone that isn't also a monster, the moment you change or dream up your Archid form, you become painfully aware that you've just been handed your shovel, and there's a mountain of shit that's piled up when your ancestors were occupied with pointless bouts of violence....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T20:27:00-07:00","id":1118813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1118710#post1118710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though, it's based on shapechanger myths, just not the traditional European Werewolf stories, so yeah, it was weird to me too, but in a good way. It was <i>different</i> form all the other werewolves in pop-culture and other rpgs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's the thing, IMO. VtM jsut covered waaay too much of the man vs. beast and infection themes too extensively for a traditional werewolf game not to be too similar. Usually, in pop-culture, werewolves are the beasts, the savages and vampires are the lords, the cool, detached nobility of the night (and usually don't have the Beast as strong as a theme, if at all, jsut bloodlust. The struggle with the inner beast is a werewolf theme, mostly.), that's why the usual urban fantasy stuff could work, but VtM had the Gangrel and the Brujah and all those things, so how traditional werewolves could have been different enough to justify it?<br /> <br /> That said, I do miss traditional werevolves from WoD. Credit where credit's due, NWoD did some very nice things and the &quot;Skinchangers&quot; book was among them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What did you think about the Hermetics?<br /> <br /> Also, honestly, I think Mages are more sorcerers, than wizards. Funnily, Sorcerers are more like D&amp;D wizards, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages are more like folkloric witches, suffering three-fold for abusing their powers and violating the natural order. Sorcerers and D&amp;D Wizards are both examples of what I think of as Alternate-Engineers. That is, they are part of a world in Hermetic practices are scientifically valid, and experimentation is done in the context of Hermetic practices being an alternate form of engineering.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T06:58:35-07:00","id":1118940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1118710#post1118710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> What did you think about the Hermetics?<br /> <br /> Also, honestly, I think Mages are more sorcerers, than wizards. Funnily, Sorcerers are more like D&amp;D wizards, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, and about Hermetics: I wasn't happy with them.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that I had come from Ars Magica, were things like grimoires, special ingredients, and magical lore, mean something. To the point that it makes sense to risk your life to get them.<br /> <br /> I was deeply offended with the idea that all my magical knowledge was just &quot;my Paradigm&quot;, that all my mage studies were meaningless outside her little fantasy.<br /> <br /> For instance. If grimoire it's more of a placebo (a Focus) than a fountain of knowledge (Grimoires weren't a thing back then), then why should I spend my time and resources trying to get one?. It felt unjust that I needed to find and study a rare ancient grimoire while an Orphan could just grab a newspeper and get the same gains for his &quot;research&quot; . It felt like I had to work extra hard just because my mage wasn't aware that all that &quot;knowledge&quot; was bullshit.<br /> <br /> Now I'm still wrestling to find even small amounts of validity in mage researches, treating Paradigm as a tool and a framework where knowledge can fit rather than knowledge itself. Magical lore isn't meaningless per se, but rather codified in a &quot;languaje&quot; that doesn't make sense for other Paradigms, including that of current reality. And I cherish Grimoires being a thing. Others surely think different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 07-21-2017, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T08:12:40-07:00","id":1118968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1118940#post1118940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, and about Hermetics: I wasn't happy with them.<br /> <br /> Keep in mind that I had come from Ars Magica, were things like grimoires, special ingredients, and magical lore, mean something. To the point that it makes sense to risk your life to get them.<br /> <br /> I was deeply offended with the idea that all my magical knowledge was just &quot;my Paradigm&quot;, that all my mage studies were meaningless outside her little fantasy.<br /> <br /> For instance. If grimoire it's more of a placebo (a Focus) than a fountain of knowledge (Grimoires weren't a thing back then), then why should I spend my time and resources trying to get one?. It felt unjust that I needed to find and study a rare ancient grimoire while an Orphan could just grab a newspeper and get the same gains for his &quot;research&quot; . It felt like I had to work extra hard just because my mage wasn't aware that all that &quot;knowledge&quot; was bullshit.<br /> <br /> Now I'm still wrestling to find even small amounts of validity in mage researches, treating Paradigm as a tool and a framework where knowledge can fit rather than knowledge itself. Magical lore isn't meaningless per se, but rather codified in a &quot;languaje&quot; that doesn't make sense for other Paradigms, including that of current reality. And I cherish Grimoires being a thing. Others surely think different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I found that soured me on playing Hermetics as well. All that work and study to achieve the same results as Hollow mixing a lot of pop garbage, or a Celestial doing some simple prayers or blessings??<br /> Oddly, I still find Sons of Ether to be tremendous fun despite the same complaint being even more true of them. There is something really fun about playing a nutty professor building crazy gadgets, even if another character can achieve the same results by doing little more than praying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T00:44:59-07:00","id":1119202,"title":"","content":"I never had much desire to play Werewolf, mainly because the emphasis on combat is so high. Games with a lot of combat are paradoxically boring to me, because characters have to be so resilient that individual combats feel low-stakes. I like that in Hunters Hunted (What is this HtR you speak of) and Mage you can get gunned down by a basic security guard in a couple turns.<br /> <br /> But Werewolf's heavy-handed environmentalism is actually a selling point for me. It treats the Holocene Extinction as a true apocalypse--which I find fascinating because it is so easy to dismiss from a civilized human perspective, yet actually valid if you think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","user":"Faradn","date":". 07-22-2017, 03:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T07:36:49-07:00","id":1119243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1119202#post1119202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never had much desire to play Werewolf, mainly because the emphasis on combat is so high. Games with a lot of combat are paradoxically boring to me, because characters have to be so resilient that individual combats feel low-stakes. I like that in Hunters Hunted (What is this HtR you speak of) and Mage you can get gunned down by a basic security guard in a couple turns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counterpoint: Being gunned down quickly is not generally the province of playing a monster, or selling point for a game where you play one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Werewolf's heavy-handed environmentalism is actually a selling point for me. It treats the Holocene Extinction as a true apocalypse--which I find fascinating because it is so easy to dismiss from a civilized human perspective, yet actually valid if you think about it. </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't use the C word to describe who brushes it off. A lot of people are set to get flooded off their islands in the Pacific, swept out, or drowned by the rising sea level, for example, and it isn't a far-off thing for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T08:01:01-07:00","id":1119246,"title":"","content":"For classic World of Darkness? I'd have to say Changeling.<br /> <br /> 1 - It is the only splat in the game which makes me feel genuinely depressed about life. The coming of age narrative and loss of childhood innocence is a little too uncomfortable for me.<br /> <br /> 2 - It's a foregone conclusion that your character is pretty much doomed regardless of how hard they struggle. If they don't succumb to banality, they'll eventually be shunned and ostracized by mortals who think they're mentally unstable.<br /> <br /> The other splats at least have a fighting chance, but Changelings are faced with a lose-lose situation.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T10:12:03-07:00","id":1119273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1119243#post1119243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Counterpoint: Being gunned down quickly is not generally the province of playing a monster, or selling point for a game where you play one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mind the toughness of Vampire characters, because it's less about combat and more about hunting prey. And that presents interesting challenges not so much in the physically overpowering, but in the masquerade aspect. Living among your prey and not getting found out. The monstrous aspect of werewolves seems more abstract to me, but I'm sure that's just personal taste.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1119243#post1119243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't use the C word to describe who brushes it off. A lot of people are set to get flooded off their islands in the Pacific, swept out, or drowned by the rising sea level, for example, and it isn't a far-off thing for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a lot of people in developed countries take global warming seriously, especially if they live on a coastal city. I was referring specifically to the plummeting biodiversity caused by human activities, where it seems the prevailing response is &quot;meh.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T10:28:17-07:00","id":1119281,"title":"","content":"Kindred are not that tough compared to Garou (though they tend to fair better against bullets).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T10:54:49-07:00","id":1119288,"title":"","content":"I like things about all the splats, but if I had to choose a least favorite it would the Rokea for their lack of relatability and the difficulty of telling engaging stories with them as heroes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T04:02:57-07:00","id":1124242,"title":"","content":"I used to love Mage, and then the M20 Corebook told me that I could use roleplaying to explore themes of the Other, like Gender Identity and Race... and to be honest that ruined the whole of Mage for me. Personally I don't like it when a book suggests themes I could explore in a mature way, it upsets me. Mage is about cosmic fluidity, exploring power and shifts in reality, questioning what it means to be human, with entire groups of Mages obsessed with questioning rigid social norms, taboos etc...<br /> <br /> *gender-related ambiguity in Mage takes up a tiny fraction of the corebook*<br /> <br /> No, not like <b><u><i>THAT</i></u></b>?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-03-2017, 07:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T05:24:42-07:00","id":1124254,"title":"","content":"I've had trouble with Changeling. I know that part of the theme is that they don't belong anymore, the Banality and all that, but they feel thematically out of step. For me Changelings were a casualty of time; Fae still exist but are powerful, alien and inhuman. Them appearing in our realm is a rare thing indeed. Modern WoD is an &quot;age of men&quot; situation, the Elves are long gone.<br /> <br /> Demon appeals to me, but I'd need to make some big mechanical and lore-based changes. Firstly, we should get it straight that the memories of Demon's origins are garbled and unreliable; some Demons truly believe that the Abrahamic God made them, some think that their memories of these mythic events are the result of potent mortal belief; Demons reflect Western Concepts of Demons because of the influence of Christianity on the world, basically.<br /> <br /> Same with Werewolf; this Spirit can say with certainty that it has personhood, but this is just projection on the part of personal creatures who interact with it. Spirits don't, by and large, have personhood. It's only thanks to the immense power of the Garou nation that Spirits all swear by all that's holy that everything the Garou believe is 100% true.<br /> <br /> So my personal fix for Demon and Werewolf is that a lot of the things spiritual beings (from Fallen Angels to spirits) believe is... questionable. Spirits aren't the creation of belief, but belief does shape them. Kupala would be just one example; the intense belief of a group of powerful supernaturals (potent Tzimisce Elders with their own primitive Magics) mutated the spirit of a bit of geography into a sort of blood-god-spirit. Whether Kupala was a &quot;spirit&quot; or an Earthbound is irrelevant; the faith of the Tzimisce has reshaped her.<br /> <br /> Why do I like this? It makes the true origins of everything murky. It makes people who think Abrahamic religions are bullshit more comfortable inhabiting the world; it isn't all built on something they've rejected. It leaves room for outside perspectives. Have the myths be just that; myths. A murderer was the first Vampire; was he &quot;Caine&quot;? Who knows! Demons claim that he was, but their memories aren't exactly cast-iron. Maybe Caine inspired Cain. Maybe Cain was the origin of Caine. Maybe God actually exists! Or maybe he's just a potent spirit, like all human gods. It also gives legitimacy to Werewolves (and Fera) who refuse their role in existence; they aren't fighting reality, they're fighting a system.<br /> <br /> It also means that the Setite who thinks Set = Caine and Osiris = Abel has nothing contradicting them directly in Word of God. Same for the Garou who thinks that Shifters are biological phenomena. Same for the Demon who thinks that their memories of the &quot;start of time&quot; are the trickery of some powerful ancient demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-03-2017, 08:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T05:35:47-07:00","id":1124259,"title":"","content":"I do not think that the Fera are powerful enough to sway the Incarna, much less the Celestines. The Fera are the servants of the most powerful of spirits, nor the masters of the most powerful of spirits. And I really do not mind there being an objective truth in oWoD as long as it proves that human beliefs are flawed and that humans cause most of the problems in the world (the Wyrm would be much less powerful in an equalitarian society with equitable laws and traditions).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T05:41:48-07:00","id":1124263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124259#post1124259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not think that the Fera are powerful enough to sway the Incarna, much less the Celestines. The Fera are the servants of the most powerful of spirits, nor the masters of the most powerful of spirits. And I really do not mind there being an objective truth in oWoD as long as it proves that human beliefs are flawed and that humans cause most of the problems in the world (the Wyrm would be much less powerful in an equalitarian society with equitable laws and traditions).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's less a case of them &quot;controlling&quot; the Incarna and Celestines, it's more like...<br /> <br /> Early Shifters worship Gaia. Gaia is the spirit of the Earth but lacks Personhood. Their worship gives her more and more personhood, more and more &quot;power&quot; and more and more flaws; she gains some of the flaws of those who worship her. She was powerful before, but now she actually... does stuff. Awakening something dormant in the object, very common concept in spirit magic. The same happens for the Triat, another staple of their religion. The Wyrm is taking away loved ones and naturally is disliked; it seems (to an unenlightened individual) like an enemy... and it slowly becomes one. The belief of Shifters and Kinfolk gradually warps the Wyrm into an antagonist... or it might have done. Maybe the Triat's personhood predates Shifters. The real answer is &quot;nobody knows&quot;, and that's how it should be. At the end of the day a Koldun arguing with a Theurge will be like two religious people arguing in the real world; no one has proof, and the &quot;proof&quot; that is offered up is never cast-iron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T06:45:36-07:00","id":1124280,"title":"","content":"Gaia is less the spirit of the Earth, and She is more the spirit of Life. While the interpretations of the spiritual phenomena are subjective in WtA, the nature of the spiritual phenomena is objective in WtA. I think that WtA serves an important purpose by presenting an objective truth by which the subjective beliefs of the other supernatural creatures can be compared and contrasted. If you just have subjectivity, it just becomes as a mess as everyone can be equally right or equally wrong. Of course, some people prefer subjectivity, which is why there is MtAs, though I find it to be the second most flawed and annoying gameline in oWoD after DtF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T19:29:01-07:00","id":1124587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124242#post1124242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used to love Mage, and then the M20 Corebook told me that I could use roleplaying to explore themes of the Other, like Gender Identity and Race... and to be honest that ruined the whole of Mage for me. Personally I don't like it when a book suggests themes I could explore in a mature way, it upsets me. Mage is about cosmic fluidity, exploring power and shifts in reality, questioning what it means to be human, with entire groups of Mages obsessed with questioning rigid social norms, taboos etc...<br /> <br /> *gender-related ambiguity in Mage takes up a tiny fraction of the corebook*<br /> <br /> No, not like <b><u><i>THAT</i></u></b>?!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting. So, you seen it an appealing thing that certain mage groups are &quot;obsessed with questioning rigid social norms, taboos etc...&quot;, but you were uncomfortable with the M20 corebook giving attention to &quot;playing the others&quot;? Could you extrapolate on that and what you consider &quot;exploring in a mature way&quot; the book fallen to convey, if you don't mind, because I'd rather seen it as a good thing, that it spoke about those things in the context of rpgs and mysticism and I'd like to understand why you found it bothering?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do I like this? It makes the true origins of everything murky. It makes people who think Abrahamic religions are bullshit more comfortable inhabiting the world; it isn't all built on something they've rejected. It leaves room for outside perspectives. Have the myths be just that; myths. A murderer was the first Vampire; was he &quot;Caine&quot;? Who knows! Demons claim that he was, but their memories aren't exactly cast-iron. Maybe Caine inspired Cain. Maybe Cain was the origin of Caine. Maybe God actually exists! Or maybe he's just a potent spirit, like all human gods. It also gives legitimacy to Werewolves (and Fera) who refuse their role in existence; they aren't fighting reality, they're fighting a system. </div> </div> </div>I'm staunchly not a Christian, or a religious person, but I never found it particularly irking. As you said, it's a myth. That it is an Abrahamic myth is totally fine and inevitable, since we're speaking about Western vampires, who grew up in a western culture and a lot of them during a time when Christianity was <i>the </i>truth. However, in the wast universe of WoD, I think even Caine doesn't know what cursed him, <i>if </i>there's a Caine and <i>if </i>he was cursed. That there's a thing as True faith and religious paraphernalia works for people with it? I'm okay with that, it's part of the whole vampire thing. I think too much people take the Book of Nod and other in-game references and mythology at face value.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T01:04:10-07:00","id":1124653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124587#post1124587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's interesting. So, you seen it an appealing thing that certain mage groups are &quot;obsessed with questioning rigid social norms, taboos etc...&quot;, but you were uncomfortable with the M20 corebook giving attention to &quot;playing the others&quot;? Could you extrapolate on that and what you consider &quot;exploring in a mature way&quot; the book fallen to convey, if you don't mind, because I'd rather seen it as a good thing, that it spoke about those things in the context of rpgs and mysticism and I'd like to understand why you found it bothering?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm staunchly not a Christian, or a religious person, but I never found it particularly irking. As you said, it's a myth. That it is an Abrahamic myth is totally fine and inevitable, since we're speaking about Western vampires, who grew up in a western culture and a lot of them during a time when Christianity was <i>the </i>truth. However, in the wast universe of WoD, I think even Caine doesn't know what cursed him, <i>if </i>there's a Caine and <i>if </i>he was cursed. That there's a thing as True faith and religious paraphernalia works for people with it? I'm okay with that, it's part of the whole vampire thing. I think too much people take the Book of Nod and other in-game references and mythology at face value.</div> </div> </div> </div>- I know English isn't your first language PMark, so I really don't mean this as an insult in any way shape or form, but I *may* have been applying some sarcasm when I said that. Personally I think that nothing could be more appropriate in Mage then questioning the boundaries of love, sex, gender, race etc; not at every table, not with every character, but as a side-bar on one page in the 700 page book? Of course! I was attempting to satirize people who get more offended than they should by space (often a tiny amount of space!) being devoted to these topics.<br /> <br /> - Hmm I just don't like Word of God confirming one religion or another, even if it is all fiction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-04-2017, 04:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T02:25:02-07:00","id":1124669,"title":"","content":"To summarize the issue, the problem with making Garou wrong about the Spirit World is that it guts them of all themes and story.<br /> <br /> The problem with doing the same to Demon is that it guts them of all their themes and story.<br /> <br /> I happily have the Garou and Demons both in my games with objective proof their entirely contradictory and mutually exclusive worldviews are correct.<br /> <br /> Because why not?<br /> <br /> I admit, my issue with Demon is that it's a really good premise marred by the Metaplot. The game really should have gone through another rewrite with its title changed to <b>Fallen: The Redemption</b> and made it a game about the whole idea of being spirits who are trying to regain their angelic status versus Archdemons, cultists, and Fallen who just want to wallow in the abyss. The big issue would be HOW one tried to redeem oneself with psychotic fundamentalist Reconcillers and Luciferians who were genuinely of the belief they could fix everything wrong with humanity like people always claim Lex Luthor could do without Superman.<br /> <br /> But that's how I would have played it.<br /> <br /> I also would have put alternative origin stories inside with the POSSIBILITY the Demons are just High Umbral spirits or Abrahamic Changelings.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, that does make the game just being Kuei-Jin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T02:59:46-07:00","id":1124674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124669#post1124669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To summarize the issue, the problem with making Garou wrong about the Spirit World is that it guts them of all themes and story.<br /> <br /> The problem with doing the same to Demon is that it guts them of all their themes and story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not wrong. Just not objectively, provably right.<br /> <br /> RAW WoD: &quot;Gaia exists and has given me a purpose in life; fulfilling that purpose is a good thing. What I'm doing is right and will save the world from the Wyrm's madness.&quot;<br /> <br /> My WoD: &quot;[Same]&quot; However someone with an understanding of Spirits could point out that Spirits are very susceptible to being molded by group belief, and therefore the words of spirits are about as reliable as religious texts or oral tradition; unreliable, fallable and possibly deceitful people have altered the message at different stages. The Spirit Mage would say the same to a Setite who believed the Setite origin myth, or to a Demon who thinks she was the Angel associated with the concept of Redemption at the start of time.<br /> <br /> &quot;Clara, I really do respect you, but you slumbered in that spiritual prison for aeons... don't you think that the power of Judeo-Abrahamic belief may have warped your memories as you slumbered? I'm not saying that it DEFINITELY didn't happen... but you shouldn't stake your existence on it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Memories of Vampires? Well when you're the only person who remembers an event 1000 years ago, gradually your own biases and wishful thinking creep in. Two Methesulahs who were both present at an event might have wildly different recollections; they've had centuries to lie to themselves in the meantime. The more you look at memory IRL the more you realise it's... mutable. We edit and tweak our memories regularly, we tell ourselves stories, and it's only social interaction with others who share those memories (&quot;Nanny's bathroom was avacado!&quot; &quot;No, it was blue, ask your uncles&quot;) that allows us to maintain something cohesive. Ancient Vampires lack that, and have centuries more to remember than human minds are built to remember.<br /> <br /> SO at my table everything is mysterious, and all beliefs have a kernel of truth but I will not give an OBJECTIVE &quot;you are correct&quot; to anyone. One of my Malkavians has &quot;ancestor blood&quot;, manifestations of the Malkavians who have died in her &quot;bloodline&quot;, back many Generations... are they real? Are they part of Malkav's madness? Are they copies Malkav made inside the Madness Network to keep himself company? Are they real Malkavian spirits hanging around in the network? There are no Objective answers to these questions, and that's good. Everything is ambiguous.<br /> <br /> Maybe your Werewolves and your Demons are right. Maybe they're wrong. Maybe it doesn't matter whether they're right or wrong, or maybe it's the most important thing in the universe. Regardless, it is great for the table as it allows more STUFF to exist, as there isn't some Grand Cosmology that is 100% definitely behind the scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T07:22:45-07:00","id":1124756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124674#post1124674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not wrong. Just not objectively, provably right.<br /> <br /> RAW WoD: &quot;Gaia exists and has given me a purpose in life; fulfilling that purpose is a good thing. What I'm doing is right and will save the world from the Wyrm's madness.&quot;<br /> <br /> My WoD: &quot;[Same]&quot; However someone with an understanding of Spirits could point out that Spirits are very susceptible to being molded by group belief, and therefore the words of spirits are about as reliable as religious texts or oral tradition; unreliable, fallable and possibly deceitful people have altered the message at different stages. The Spirit Mage would say the same to a Setite who believed the Setite origin myth, or to a Demon who thinks she was the Angel associated with the concept of Redemption at the start of time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf isn't the game of primal spirits being molded by belief. That's Mage, and it does it in such a way that no other game would escape the same treatment, so crossover with anything and Mage is... contentious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Clara, I really do respect you, but you slumbered in that spiritual prison for aeons... don't you think that the power of Judeo-Abrahamic belief may have warped your memories as you slumbered? I'm not saying that it DEFINITELY didn't happen... but you shouldn't stake your existence on it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Memories of Vampires? Well when you're the only person who remembers an event 1000 years ago, gradually your own biases and wishful thinking creep in. Two Methesulahs who were both present at an event might have wildly different recollections; they've had centuries to lie to themselves in the meantime. The more you look at memory IRL the more you realise it's... mutable. We edit and tweak our memories regularly, we tell ourselves stories, and it's only social interaction with others who share those memories (&quot;Nanny's bathroom was avacado!&quot; &quot;No, it was blue, ask your uncles&quot;) that allows us to maintain something cohesive. Ancient Vampires lack that, and have centuries more to remember than human minds are built to remember.<br /> <br /> SO at my table everything is mysterious, and all beliefs have a kernel of truth but I will not give an OBJECTIVE &quot;you are correct&quot; to anyone. One of my Malkavians has &quot;ancestor blood&quot;, manifestations of the Malkavians who have died in her &quot;bloodline&quot;, back many Generations... are they real? Are they part of Malkav's madness? Are they copies Malkav made inside the Madness Network to keep himself company? Are they real Malkavian spirits hanging around in the network? There are no Objective answers to these questions, and that's good. Everything is ambiguous.<br /> <br /> Maybe your Werewolves and your Demons are right. Maybe they're wrong. Maybe it doesn't matter whether they're right or wrong, or maybe it's the most important thing in the universe. Regardless, it is great for the table as it allows more STUFF to exist, as there isn't some Grand Cosmology that is 100% definitely behind the scenes. </div> </div> </div>Some games aren't built for that variety of post-modern interpretation, or Mage's. In the end, Werewolf doesn't dwell on questions of whether or not the cosmology is correct, but how they'll approach the problems of the world. It just doesn't serve the themes of Werewolf to pull the rug out from under the reader or players; it's far more likely to cause resentment, bad blood, and the breakup of a group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T07:33:50-07:00","id":1124763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124756#post1124756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf isn't the game of primal spirits being molded by belief. That's Mage, and it does it in such a way that no other game would escape the same treatment, so crossover with anything and Mage is... contentious.<br /> <br /> Some games aren't built for that variety of post-modern interpretation, or Mage's. In the end, Werewolf doesn't dwell on questions of whether or not the cosmology is correct, but how they'll approach the problems of the world. It just doesn't serve the themes of Werewolf to pull the rug out from under the reader or players; it's far more likely to cause resentment, bad blood, and the breakup of a group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not a great lover of Mage, I enjoy reading it but I've yet to play it extensively. I adopt this approach not for Mage's sake, but for the sake of Crossovers in general, and the wider universe. Things just make more sense if spirits can be shaped by belief; that's an idea that is so common pinning it to Mage is ridiculous! So much fiction about gods and spirits has them being shaped by the beliefs of those who believe in them.<br /> <br /> Does it matter though? Does it really bother a Werewolf player if the ST says &quot;what you believe is fit for the purpose of what you're supposed to do for the nation, but I cannot 100% word of god confirm that everything you believe is true... there are tonnes of Fera with alternative versions of events, and there are possibly even secrets being kept from you for your own good, some truths inspire dissent and that's a path to the Wyrm in dire times like these. In Character you believe it with all your heart, and that's a great roleplaying experience, but I'm not going to comfort you by Word-of-God-ing everything.&quot;. It's worth noting that in this version everything Werewolves believe *could still be true*, it's just not the only possible truth. This allows for coexistence of ideas, and for a wider variety of roleplaying. The Garou who rejects the concept of spiritual duty is no longer &quot;Objectively 100% Wrong and a Monster&quot;, he's just a heretic against a &quot;religion&quot; (or culture) that believes he is doing something objectively wrong. It's an important distinction which matters a lot to some people, and I'm much more patient with people who don't want to be objectively wrong than I am with people who NEED to be objectively right. One is a reasonable and mature request of the ST, one is demanding to be pandered to, to be given black and white moral clarity which is stifling to good roleplay... I don't actively dislike it, but it certainly isn't fit for my table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T07:53:02-07:00","id":1124773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124763#post1124763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not a great lover of Mage, I enjoy reading it but I've yet to play it extensively. I adopt this approach not for Mage's sake, but for the sake of Crossovers in general, and the wider universe. Things just make more sense if spirits can be shaped by belief; that's an idea that is so common pinning it to Mage is ridiculous! So much fiction about gods and spirits has them being shaped by the beliefs of those who believe in them.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, in the WoD, that's explicitly Mage's bag, and explicitly the opposite of how Werewolf works. Humans believe all sorts of things, but the truth maintained by the spirits, the souls of the world that allow it to exist in the first place, is what it is, and doesn't bend over because someone thinks that the world is actually a computer simulation that they can hack.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does it matter though? Does it really bother a Werewolf player if the ST says &quot;what you believe is fit for the purpose of what you're supposed to do for the nation, but I cannot 100% word of god confirm that everything you believe is true... there are tonnes of Fera with alternative versions of events, </div> </div> </div>Not that alternate, and it certainly doesn't change the animistic workings of Werewolf, where killing the spirit eliminates something from existence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and there are possibly even secrets being kept from you for your own good, some truths inspire dissent and that's a path to the Wyrm in dire times like these. </div> </div> </div>The truth is that the Garou have a lot of hard work to do that they aren't entirely well suited toward. In time, they can learn more from other spirits, but spirits are kind of the thing for Werewolf, and other secrets don't really enter into it. That's the game's theme and MO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Character you believe it with all your heart, and that's a great roleplaying experience, but I'm not going to comfort you by Word-of-God-ing everything.&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Again, the game runs off of certainty that the world is set up exactly the way that the book presents it, and that the spirit portion of the Garou and Fera lets them know this exactly. And it also lets them know that the world is running out of time, that the great cosmos is dying, and spirits are being torn apart in greater numbers than they should be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's worth noting that in this version everything Werewolves believe *could still be true*, it's just not the only possible truth. This allows for coexistence of ideas, and for a wider variety of roleplaying. The Garou who rejects the concept of spiritual duty is no longer &quot;Objectively 100% Wrong and a Monster&quot;, he's just a heretic against a &quot;religion&quot; (or culture) that believes he is doing something objectively wrong. It's an important distinction which matters a lot to some people, and I'm much more patient with people who don't want to be objectively wrong than I am with people who NEED to be objectively right. One is a reasonable and mature request of the ST, one is demanding to be pandered to, to be given black and white moral clarity which is stifling to good roleplay... I don't actively dislike it, but it certainly isn't fit for my table. </div> </div> </div>Garou who reject the spirits are rejecting part of themselves, since they are half spirit. Others can walk different paths, but for the Garou and Fera, the Middle Umbra is a timeless and indelible part of their core being. Whether or not they approach dealings with spirits in any way that looks like a religion is irrelevant, because their belief doesn't even matter; they can feel and touch a world just to the side of matter and flesh, and it calls out to them.<br /> <br /> This doesn't equate with absolute moral clarity, though, since there's no one to give any license to terrible things that you do, and you have to face the music for what you do. Werewolves blindly charging in time and again resulted in a long string of failures, and there's no justification or moral license given to make those &quot;right&quot; even if the society that sprang up to make sure that Garou were warriors and the highest ranking were the greatest warriors sings of too many of those rampages as if they were heroic triumphs. Therein lies the difficulty of working with your own society; in order to actually make actual headway in solving problems in the world, you have to forego many of the rampages that would provide you with power and influence due to the Renown they would garner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T13:13:40-07:00","id":1124912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124653#post1124653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - I know English isn't your first language PMark, so I really don't mean this as an insult in any way shape or form, but I *may* have been applying some sarcasm when I said that. Personally I think that nothing could be more appropriate in Mage then questioning the boundaries of love, sex, gender, race etc; not at every table, not with every character, but as a side-bar on one page in the 700 page book? Of course! I was attempting to satirize people who get more offended than they should by space (often a tiny amount of space!) being devoted to these topics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay, understood! It was just confusing at first that it seemed you thought those topics are important, but had a problem with the book giving them attention. I thought you might thought it wasn't enough or didn't like how and what Brucatto wrote, or something like that and I was curious about it.<br /> <br /> Personally, I liked that part of the book, I think those topics are appropriate for Mage (although not primary topics - for me). It wasn't a problem to me that the book was &quot;too political&quot; as certain people thought, for various reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> - Hmm I just don't like Word of God confirming one religion or another, even if it is all fiction. </div> </div> </div>I understand, me neither. That's part of my problem with Demon. However, I never felt that Vampire proves unarguably the existence of an Abrahamic God, or that those religions are right. We just have some phenomenon, sun burns, true faith works, etc, but we don't really know the reasons. Of course Western vampires explained it through the lens of Abrahamic religions, but even if there is/was <i>a </i>Caine and even if some entity cursed him with vampirism, that could have been a lot of things. Ultimately, what we really know is that the clans have progenitors and that vampires in general have some mystical banes. That's all, everything else is mythology.<br /> <br /> It never got explored much I think, but it'd be interesting to see what truly ancient methuselahs, those who hailed from eras long before Christianity think about it? What were their origin stories?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:16:19-07:00","id":1124938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124912#post1124912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand, me neither. That's part of my problem with Demon. However, I never felt that Vampire proves unarguably the existence of an Abrahamic God, or that those religions are right. We just have some phenomenon, sun burns, true faith works, etc, but we don't really know the reasons. Of course Western vampires explained it through the lens of Abrahamic religions, but even if there is/was <i>a </i>Caine and even if some entity cursed him with vampirism, that could have been a lot of things. Ultimately, what we really know is that the clans have progenitors and that vampires in general have some mystical banes. That's all, everything else is mythology.<br /> <br /> It never got explored much I think, but it'd be interesting to see what truly ancient methuselahs, those who hailed from eras long before Christianity think about it? What were their origin stories?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well I confirm that there is a &quot;first Vampire&quot;, and that they were a person who murdered their sibling and were punished as a result, but whether this was literally the Cain and Abel story is up for debate. It could be Set and Osiris, as just one example, or it could be a memetic theme in all religions (floods and the two brothers fighting crops up in a lot of origin myths) as a result of some profound meta-myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:19:56-07:00","id":1124940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124756#post1124756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolf isn't the game of primal spirits being molded by belief. That's Mage, and it does it in such a way that no other game would escape the same treatment, so crossover with anything and Mage is... contentious.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Some games aren't built for that variety of post-modern interpretation, or Mage's. In the end, Werewolf doesn't dwell on questions of whether or not the cosmology is correct, but how they'll approach the problems of the world. It just doesn't serve the themes of Werewolf to pull the rug out from under the reader or players; it's far more likely to cause resentment, bad blood, and the breakup of a group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno, I always treated WoD as no one's objectively right, just as 11twiggins wrote, but everyone has some part of the truth. What mages know about consensual reality is just a part of the whole, just like what Garou know about Gaia and the Triat, or what the other Fera, or Mummies, or vampired Demons, etc know. For me, it works.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 08-04-2017, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:24:43-07:00","id":1124942,"title":"","content":"There is no 'proof' of a first Kindred, just legends and myths like those found in any culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:33:29-07:00","id":1124949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124938#post1124938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well I confirm that there is a &quot;first Vampire&quot;, and that they were a person who murdered their sibling and were punished as a result, but whether this was literally the Cain and Abel story is up for debate. It could be Set and Osiris, as just one example, or it could be a memetic theme in all religions (floods and the two brothers fighting crops up in a lot of origin myths) as a result of some profound meta-myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing: we don't even know if there was a &quot;first vampire&quot;. We know about the progenitors and that's all. The Setite's story strictly contradicts to the Caine myth. Yes, generations are numbered, sot we could see it as a definite, objective truth, but really in my eyes that's not the case even, it just reflects the things vampires think and know today. So, even the existence of a &quot;Caine&quot; is more like a high probability in my mind, given the generations and all that, but not a surety and aside from that? I agree nobody knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:42:53-07:00","id":1124952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124949#post1124949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's the thing: we don't even know if there was a &quot;first vampire&quot;. We know about the progenitors and that's all. The Setite's story strictly contradicts to the Caine myth. Yes, generations are numbered, sot we could see it as a definite, objective truth, but really in my eyes that's not the case even, it just reflects the things vampires think and know today. So, even the existence of a &quot;Caine&quot; is more like a high probability in my mind, given the generations and all that, but not a surety and aside from that? I agree nobody knows.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes even a single Vampire isn't 100% certain, you have Mages saying that Vampirism originated with 13 potent Archmages attempting to ascend to a perfect form of Lichdom; they can only survive by draining Quintessence (via blood) and they are facing a horrific Paradox backlash (burning in sunlight among other things). Generations are numbered based on the assumption that the Caine myth is real; the 3rd Generation would be the &quot;1st Generation&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T15:20:26-07:00","id":1124968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124952#post1124952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well yes even a single Vampire isn't 100% certain, you have Mages saying that Vampirism originated with 13 potent Archmages attempting to ascend to a perfect form of Lichdom; they can only survive by draining Quintessence (via blood) and they are facing a horrific Paradox backlash (burning in sunlight among other things). Generations are numbered based on the assumption that the Caine myth is real; the 3rd Generation would be the &quot;1st Generation&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and Setites are counting generations differently, Assamites too. <br /> <br /> Where that mage-theory was written? I seen it several times on the forums, but can't remember reading it in a book. Also, i could imagine a version of it even for the Caine-mythos. Caine was a mage attempting to reach eternal life and Abel was his brother, who got ultimately sacrificed in a ritual for &quot;a&quot; god and it went horribly wrong. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T15:50:11-07:00","id":1124984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124968#post1124968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where that mage-theory was written? I seen it several times on the forums, but can't remember reading it in a book. Also, i could imagine a version of it even for the Caine-mythos. Caine was a mage attempting to reach eternal life and Abel was his brother, who got ultimately sacrificed in a ritual for &quot;a&quot; god and it went horribly wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no idea. I imagine in Mage: Revised at some point, but I've only seen it on these forums. That's a great idea though! Personally I wouldn't run with it since Lilith as the &quot;Mother of Magic&quot; is a powerful image for me, but I can see it working.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T16:01:10-07:00","id":1124991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124984#post1124984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no idea. I imagine in Mage: Revised at some point, but I've only seen it on these forums. That's a great idea though! Personally I wouldn't run with it since Lilith as the &quot;Mother of Magic&quot; is a powerful image for me, but I can see it working.</div> </div> </div> </div>The whole Lilith thing is very interesting. I like it and that it has even less actual information than the Caine myth despite paths and factions based on beliefs around her. I mean, there aren't even something like the generations to back it up. What Lilith was, if she even was is a totally open question and it's the best for it.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think she was an even older, more primordial something, maybe one of the earliest, if not the earliest human being practicing awakened magic and warped by it, who pissed off some entities, maybe the one what cursed Caine and she probably mentored Caine, at some point.<br /> <br /> Or maybe she was an Earthbound. Or a true Fae.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T18:15:04-07:00","id":1125032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1124940#post1124940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dunno, I always treated WoD as no one's objectively right, just as 11twiggins wrote, but everyone has some part of the truth. What mages know about consensual reality is just a part of the whole, just like what Garou know about Gaia and the Triat, or what the other Fera, or Mummies, or vampired Demons, etc know. For me, it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that consensus is wholly unique to Mage. Even the closest other thing to have it, Changeling, doesn't actually have it, since while the Dreaming does rely heavily on human glamour, the reality without glamour is not affected by belief. I'd hardly call consensual reality a piece of &quot;the greater truth&quot; if it never joins with &quot;other truths&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T18:38:18-07:00","id":1125041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1125032#post1125032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that consensus is wholly unique to Mage. Even the closest other thing to have it, Changeling, doesn't actually have it, since while the Dreaming does rely heavily on human glamour, the reality without glamour is not affected by belief. I'd hardly call consensual reality a piece of &quot;the greater truth&quot; if it never joins with &quot;other truths&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I said it's just a part of the truth. I'm a staunch supporter of the &quot;consensus isn't absolute&quot; opinion and the Mythic Threads concept from M20, so there it is. I just don't see any of the games' worldviews as mutually exclusive. They're just like that, if taken to the extreme and taking as absolute truths. You're a Werewolf purist (I apologize if that's an offensive surmise to you), so you see it differently and that's okay too.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T18:53:16-07:00","id":1125045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1125041#post1125041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I said it's just a part of the truth. I'm a staunch supporter of the &quot;consensus isn't absolute&quot; opinion and the Mythic Threads concept from M20, so there it is. I just don't see any of the games' worldviews as mutually exclusive. They're just like that, if taken to the extreme and taking as absolute truths. You're a <b>Werewolf purist</b> (I apologize if that's an offensive surmise to you), so you see it differently and that's okay too.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I just don't like Vampire, Mage, Demon, or the &quot;no one really knows&quot; standpoint, really. Even if you dropped me in a game that had nothing to do with Werewolf, I would find that last point extremely aggravating to hear. Especially repeatedly, for the entire time that I was engaged with the fandom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T22:52:04-07:00","id":1125112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1125045#post1125045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I just don't like Vampire, Mage, Demon, or the &quot;no one really knows&quot; standpoint, really. Even if you dropped me in a game that had nothing to do with Werewolf, I would find that last point extremely aggravating to hear. Especially repeatedly, for the entire time that I was engaged with the fandom.</div> </div> </div> </div>*shrug* So just make werewolf the correct worldview when you are running games. Vampires are Wyrmspawn who drain gnosis via blood. Mages are insane reality-warpers who misinterpret their ability to unleash the wyld or strengthen the weaver with &quot;Ascension&quot;. Etc, etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T06:13:53-07:00","id":1125190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1125112#post1125112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *shrug* So just make werewolf the correct worldview when you are running games. Vampires are Wyrmspawn who drain gnosis via blood. Mages are insane reality-warpers who misinterpret their ability to unleash the wyld or strengthen the weaver with &quot;Ascension&quot;. Etc, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires don't have or interact with Gnosis (they're spiritually dead, after all), and mages have nothing to do with the Triat.(humans are not tuned into these things, and Mage is tuned into itself first and foremost).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T07:57:45-07:00","id":1125221,"title":"","content":"*sigh* I said &quot;make&quot; the werewolf worldview correct, i.e. houserule things to fit the other systems fit as an extension of werewolf, if that's the worldview you prefer to be correct.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T08:47:42-07:00","id":1125244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1125112#post1125112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> *shrug* So just make werewolf the correct worldview when you are running games. Vampires are Wyrmspawn who drain gnosis via blood. Mages are insane reality-warpers who misinterpret their ability to unleash the wyld or strengthen the weaver with &quot;Ascension&quot;. Etc, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean I see the appeal of knowing exactly what is what (Garou Lore is largely correct, the other Fera are largely correct), I just think that if you want that kind of clarity you'd be better off playing something that isn't set in the World of Darkness. The Shifters are, at the end of the day, monsters. They have lore-based justification for all the fucked up stuff they do (murdering sentient creatures, eco-terrorism, treatment of non-complying Garou which borders on Genocide, they have an entire sea of silver in the Umbra to &quot;correct&quot; Garou whose triat alignment doesn't fit the norm), and that does excuse a lot of it. They don't have time to be nice; if they hesitate then everything will be ruined forever, it may already be too late. But they are still monsters when all is said and done, and their beliefs cannot be objectively proven... they're effectively religious fundamentalists, with spirits acting as part of their oral tradition and giving a *modicum* of extra clarity. The idea that the Garou know what's what is a naive conceit, and someone who wants the comfortable &quot;don't worry you're right about everything&quot; approach isn't going to fit in at my table.<br /> <br /> But Golden Rule, hey ho. If people enjoy a morally unambiguous tale where furry eco-terrorists do That Which Must Be Done to save the world (with all who disagree being Objectively Wrong and The Worst; looking at you, Garou who just want to live their lives and not fight a holy war, you awful fucks!), then at least they're enjoying themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-05-2017, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T10:45:43-07:00","id":1125276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1125244#post1125244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean I see the appeal of knowing exactly what is what (Garou Lore is largely correct, the other Fera are largely correct), I just think that if you want that kind of clarity you'd be better off playing something that isn't set in the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have the strangest qualifiers for what goes into a setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Shifters are, at the end of the day, monsters. </div> </div> </div>That was the entire point of these games. To have a space where you place monsters. Monsters, mind you, take many forms other than cursed, blood-drinking corpses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have lore-based justification for all the fucked up stuff they do </div> </div> </div>No, they have lore-based motivations. Violence is the easiest road to approaching problems for Garou and many Fera, so it gets used an awful lot, like in Exalted. And like in Exalted, it makes an awful tangle of the world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (murdering sentient creatures </div> </div> </div>Do you even know what that word means in an ethical framework? Because it gets distorted a lot between pop culture speculative fiction and the one used in ethics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> eco-terrorism, treatment of non-complying Garou which borders on Genocide, they have an entire sea of silver in the Umbra to &quot;correct&quot; Garou whose triat alignment doesn't fit the norm) </div> </div> </div>As editions have gone on, excuses have dried up and left; killing is killing even if you get Glory from it. Also, Erebus isn't really a common destination for anyone leaning to any part of the Triat. Usually, they tip over and fall into other realms, like Malfeas, the abode of the OneSong, or parts unknown long before anyone thinks to use the Rite of the Silver Forge. Which doesn't even actually do anything, apparently, unless the Garou being tossed in wants it to, as of W20.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They don't have time to be nice </div> </div> </div>But it would have helped a lot if they had learned to use softer touches in the past, so says all of their errors.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> if they hesitate then everything will be ruined forever, it may already be too late. </div> </div> </div>Usually the sort of tense situations that induce frenzies are way more personal than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But they are still monsters when all is said and done, and their beliefs cannot be objectively proven... they're effectively religious fundamentalists, with spirits acting as part of their oral tradition and giving a *modicum* of extra clarity. The idea that the Garou know what's what is a naive conceit, and someone who wants the comfortable &quot;don't worry you're right about everything&quot; approach isn't going to fit in at my table. </div> </div> </div>Here we get back into the problem - they aren't beliefs. Beliefs don't have the capacity to punch you in the face on their lonesome. Spirits are a fact of life in Werewolf, and they allow the physical world to exist in the setting. Also, this fact isn't really a definite form of comfort, because you're the one charged with taking care of things when they go wrong. And they will go wrong. So very, very wrong. Spirits with opposing correspondences and bents can get into feuds that embroil Garou and Fera allies. Spirits also are likely to need defense from encroachment, absorption, or devouring by various antagonists, but if you spend all your time in the Umbra, you'll lose your flesh and go from half spirit to all spirit.<br /> <br /> Is what you have to do clear? More or less. Is it easy to manage it? No, because in addition to that duty, you have your life to live in between missions, quests, or whatever it is that you want to call the many dangerous situations that won't leave you alone even if you tried.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But Golden Rule, hey ho. If people enjoy a morally unambiguous tale where furry eco-terrorists do That Which Must Be Done to save the world (with all who disagree being Objectively Wrong and The Worst; looking at you, Garou who just want to live their lives and not fight a holy war, you awful fucks!), then at least they're enjoying themselves. </div> </div> </div>I spent this post and a previous one explaining that it wasn't actually morally unambiguous by a long shot. Also, why are you, here, getting on the case of the Garou for not giving others of their kind a chance to &quot;live their own lives&quot; when one of the other parts of the WoD tends to revolve around societies that dictate what and how you do things?<br /> <br /> Edit: And clarity isn't really a problem; it just adds another dimension to complications. The sorcerer-kings in Dark Sun, and the Dragon of Tyr, are keeping an even worse evil imprisoned away from Athas, but that doesn't mean that they have the best way to do it. The goal of heroes in that setting, if given to a bent of trying to make the world a better place, is to find a better system to replace the &quot;immortal energy-sucking wizards send 1000 slaves every year as sacrifices to the super energy-sucking dragon to ritually bind Rajaat&quot; setup with something that doesn't require you, too, to be a shitty asshole perpetuating the system. Obviously, many of the specifics will differ in Werewolf and other WoD games, but the distinction is sound.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 08-05-2017, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T11:58:54-07:00","id":1125295,"title":"","content":"A world where your fundamental duties are uncertain it's as asinine to Werewolf as an objective world where duties are certain and science it's true it's to Mage.<br /> <br /> The reason it's that the game it's supposed to be one of epic struggles. If the wyrm isn't objectively wrong nor a danger to the universe, then the stakes are much lower. The game isn't about stopping apocalypse anymore, because that's now uncertain. The game it's called Werewolf: The Apocalipse, not Werewolf: The Paranoic Religion, I imaginge werewolf players enjoy their struggle to save the world as much as vampire players enjoy the Yihad, and wouldn't want the main issue of the game to be relativized to open the possibility to play werewolves that &quot;are against the system&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, if science it's right and mages can't do anything to change that, then Ascencion War cannot be won and the game looses one of it's main themes.<br /> <br /> I think that relativity can be ported to Werewolf, but not that way: Werewolves can't be wrong about the state of the world nor about the need of stopping the Wyrm, but they may be wrong about their methods, about the nature of the corruption.<br /> For instance:<br /> Rat and Bear Incarna lived for millenia without loosing their grasp on the reality, largely unchanged by &quot;belief&quot;, they both know that the world was balanced in the past, and it was much better, both know about the corruption of the Wyrm (and, as Gaian, would want to fight it), but if asked how to defeat the Wyrm, they will have very different answers: Rat has the perspective of rats about the Wyrm and how to deal with problems, and Bear has, likely, another perspective. Both may be wrong, mind you, spirits don't know everything<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Golden Rule, hey ho. If people enjoy a morally unambiguous tale where furry eco-terrorists do That Which Must Be Done to save the world (with all who disagree being Objectively Wrong and The Worst; looking at you, Garou who just want to live their lives and not fight a holy war, you awful fucks!), then at least they're enjoying themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may be wrong about *who* it's invoking the golden rule here. You're the one that's disregading the canon ooc lore of the game declaring it's lame, and then changing it for the purposes of your table (legit use of the Golden Rule if your players have no objection). Werewolf isn't a game about playing a Ronin, it doesn't present &quot;ronin&quot; as a cool rebelious concept for the stereotypical PC, you are changing that bacause you think your way it's cooler.<br /> <br /> If the core premises of the game are respected, &quot;Garou who just want to live their lives and not fight a holy war&quot; would be slaped in the face by reality. Look at the people that relativize climate change, well your rebelious Garou would be just like that, telling everyone that the Wyrm causing the apocalypse it's just a superstition, while watching how the devourer grows nastier and nastier all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-05-2017, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:59:29-07:00","id":1125368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1125295#post1125295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that relativity can be ported to Werewolf, but not that way: Werewolves can't be wrong about the state of the world nor about the need of stopping the Wyrm, but they may be wrong about their methods, about the nature of the corruption.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I don't get is how bringing in the other lines' viewpoints end up as werewolves being wrong about the state of the world and the Wyrm? I don't think they are wrong, I just think the others are largely unconcerned and that Werewolves are much more involved with spirits and certain aspects of the Umbra and see the workings of spirits a bit differently than mages.<br /> <br /> Ok, the Wyrm is real, the problem is real, but most mages don't know about the depth of it. They're encountering with banes sometimes, which they probably see as a problem, but a localized one. So, most of them are unaware of the bigger picture. However, Garou on the other hand try to fit into their worldview everything and some round pegs just won't get into square holes. Like that the Triat and Gaia aren't the only forces of the universe. Nobody gets the full picture. There's the Triat itself, for example. Mages are recognizing those cosmic forces and calling them stasis/entropy/dynamism, but that doesn't mean that their view is more right than the Garou's.<br /> <br /> That the werewolves fight isn't the one and only important thing in the world and that other splats have their own concerns, or that the werewolves worldview isn't absolute and all-encompassing doesn't make their fight less significant, or their world less intriguing to me.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T18:41:35-07:00","id":1125441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1125368#post1125368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What I don't get is how bringing in the other lines' viewpoints end up as werewolves being wrong about the state of the world and the Wyrm? I don't think they are wrong, I just think the others are largely unconcerned and that Werewolves are much more involved with spirits and certain aspects of the Umbra and see the workings of spirits a bit differently than mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Aleph pointed out in the very first line of the post that you quoted, Werewolf and Mage tend toward immiscibility. They have more or less mutually exclusive setups of the cosmos relative to each other, and their themes are starkly at odds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ok, the Wyrm is real, the problem is real, but most mages don't know about the depth of it. They're encountering with banes sometimes, which they probably see as a problem, but a localized one. So, most of them are unaware of the bigger picture. </div> </div> </div>And their game is also predicated on the cosmos not actually being in danger. It has an unbridled expectation that humanity, through the Awakened, can make it work by looking at all these different viewpoints. Werewolf is considerably more... grounded in what's required.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, Garou on the other hand try to fit into their worldview everything and some round pegs just won't get into square holes. </div> </div> </div>The way that the cosmos works in Werewolf doesn't have nearly so many unfixed points, so it works for them. While there may be blind spots for Garou and Fera, they aren't necessarily missing pieces of a puzzle as they might be in Mage; more likely, the unknowns are just not going to be any help, at best, and might get persuaded by their enemies to move against them at the other end. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Like that the Triat and Gaia aren't the only forces of the universe. Nobody gets the full picture. There's the Triat itself, for example. Mages are recognizing those cosmic forces and calling them stasis/entropy/dynamism, but that doesn't mean that their view is more right than the Garou's. </div> </div> </div>But the Triat and the Trinity aren't the same thing (The Wyrm was Balance, is now maddened and its lower pieces from Celestine on down act as Corruption instead), and forces associated with &quot;Dynamism&quot; weren't pushed into the Umbra before leaking out in Mage, at least as far as I can tell.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That the werewolves fight isn't the one and only important thing in the world and that other splats have their own concerns, or that the werewolves worldview isn't absolute and all-encompassing doesn't make their fight less significant, or their world less intriguing to me. </div> </div> </div>That might be doable, but all the different games (yes, even Mage) present a very strong theme that doesn't have very much wiggle room for the other games. Well, maybe not Hunter, since its theme is &quot;formerly unknowing humans get tossed in the deep end and have to deal with it&quot;, and that does leave more space to move around as long as you don't try to shackle it to Demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T19:14:13-07:00","id":1125455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1125441#post1125441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Aleph pointed out in the very first line of the post that you quoted, Werewolf and Mage tend toward immiscibility. They have more or less mutually exclusive setups of the cosmos relative to each other, and their themes are starkly at odds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where you see mutual exclusivity I see different focus. Werewolves don't have to be uncertain about their duty to work with mages in the same story. Also, I don't see the two games' cosmoses being that different, just perceived differently and accentuating different aspects. Moreover, I don't think their themes at odds, they just have different themes, but can work alongside.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And their game is also predicated on the cosmos not actually being in danger. It has an unbridled expectation that humanity, through the Awakened, can make it work by looking at all these different viewpoints. Werewolf is considerably more... grounded in what's required. </div> </div> </div>In my eyes, werewolves have a very specific viewpoint and cause to exist. Mages just don't share that and have other concerns. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way that the cosmos works in Werewolf doesn't have nearly so many unfixed points, so it works for them. While there may be blind spots for Garou and Fera, they aren't necessarily missing pieces of a puzzle as they might be in Mage; more likely, the unknowns are just not going to be any help, at best, and might get persuaded by their enemies to move against them at the other end. </div> </div> </div>Again, they have a very focused view. Some things they see more in depth than mages, some things, they have less clue about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the Triat and the Trinity aren't the same thing (The Wyrm was Balance, is now maddened and its lower pieces from Celestine on down act as Corruption instead), and forces associated with &quot;Dynamism&quot; weren't pushed into the Umbra before leaking out in Mage, at least as far as I can tell. </div> </div> </div>They aren't the same, but they are the same principles. Arguably, the Wyrm was balance by Entropy, by grinding away the excesses. I think mages realized that, but they don't know how horribly wrong it came to be. Also, werewolves are speaking about the Triat as cosmic beings, why mages are speaking about the trinity as metaphysical concepts. Both are aspects of the same principles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That might be doable, but all the different games (yes, even Mage) present a very strong theme that doesn't have very much wiggle room for the other games. </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, IMO. You and a lot of others don't like mixing up things, because don't want other games thematic elements to intrude upon any specific game's own playground and giving up any of the splats' state as the center of the game's universe, seeing it as sacrificing its own themes. And/or don't want to bend the specific games' metaphysics even in the least. I understand that, it's a legit way to see things, but to me, it's a bit similar to how hardliner fans of specific kinds of fantasy can't abide firearms, rapiers and other renaissance stuff in a Tolkienesque fantasy. For me, mixing things, to provide a larger plethora of potential stories and themes is a good thing and I just never saw the gamelines going as starkly against each other and being as mutually exclusive as some of you. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T07:38:16-07:00","id":1125590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1125455#post1125455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where you see mutual exclusivity I see different focus. Werewolves don't have to be uncertain about their duty to work with mages in the same story. Also, I don't see the two games' cosmoses being that different, just perceived differently and accentuating different aspects. Moreover, I don't think their themes at odds, they just have different themes, but can work alongside.</div> </div> </div> </div>The very first thing that the crossover section of the Revised W:tA ST Handbook mentions is the incompatible underlying themes. Mage has humans as the center of the cosmos, and has reality altered by sufficient human belief. Werewolf fundamentally rejects both of these, and whether or not you choose to houserule it, it's a very big difference, and the text also notes that either game is going to suffer for crossing over with the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Again, they have a very focused view. Some things they see more in depth than mages, some things, they have less clue about. </div> </div> </div>Because they occur in outright different settings. One of them is animistic to the core and the other relies on strong beliefs and mythic threads. Spirit mages in a game where you use Werewolf's cosmology as-is would be all-powerful and everyone else would be chumps for specializing in any other Sphere. This is one reason why they do not get along.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They aren't the same, but they are the same principles. Arguably, the Wyrm was balance by Entropy, by grinding away the excesses. I think mages realized that, but they don't know how horribly wrong it came to be. Also, werewolves are speaking about the Triat as cosmic beings, why mages are speaking about the trinity as metaphysical concepts. Both are aspects of the same principles. </div> </div> </div>Mage doesn't even usually acknowledge that they're in opposition. Stasis isn't trying to trap Entropy in Mage, in any manner, but you'd see that in Werewolf in much more concrete style, because the spirits cause reality to exist in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's the thing, IMO. You and a lot of others don't like mixing up things, because don't want other games thematic elements to intrude upon any specific game's own playground and giving up any of the splats' state as the center of the game's universe, seeing it as sacrificing its own themes. And/or don't want to bend the specific games' metaphysics even in the least. I understand that, it's a legit way to see things, but to me, it's a bit similar to how hardliner fans of specific kinds of fantasy can't abide firearms, rapiers and other renaissance stuff in a Tolkienesque fantasy. For me, mixing things, to provide a larger plethora of potential stories and themes is a good thing and I just never saw the gamelines going as starkly against each other and being as mutually exclusive as some of you.<br /> </div> </div> </div>I don't want Mage's thematic elements anywhere near a game i'm playing, no. And your entreaty to consider the potential stories falls flat for me, because I didn't get into Werewolf or Changeling for some nonsense involving space battles around Jupiter, only it's really the spirit world for some reason, and there are orbital prisons that are holding Harry and Hermione captive. Also, the system itself rubs me the wrong way, and not just because of a really weird power curve, but because it irons out all the interesting differences between every approach that exists. While Vampire and Demon have their pitfalls and bizarre crossover rules, trying to convince me that a flamethrower is actually like a fireball spell is not one of them.<br /> <br /> As for D&amp;D, I don't care what you put in your pseudo-Tolkienesque Forgotten Realms game. Just make sure to use the 1e DMG Boot Hill conversion for guns; the 5e DMG is out of order in making pistols do damage on par with muskets. Though admittedly archaic, the musket's damaging effect is often compared to a shotgun slug.<br /> <br /> (NB: I just referenced one of the least D&amp;D-like D&amp;D settings a few posts ago, so the fantasy hardliner thing made be chuckle a bit.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T10:13:20-07:00","id":1125624,"title":"","content":"In terms of game lines? Demon: the Fallen. It's painfully early 2000's NuMetal edgelord doofishness. Like you open the front cover and Powerman 5000's &quot;When Worlds Collide&quot; begins playing. So not my taste.<br /> <br /> From specific splats... any of the multitudes of &quot;emotionally dead&quot; splat types - True brujah (though V20 seems to have fixed this), Ananasi, Nagah, stuff like that. &quot;Emotionally dead&quot; was sort of WW's shorthand for &quot;alien&quot; or &quot;grim&quot; and all it really amounted to is &quot;If you're roleplaying this at all, you're roleplaying it incorrectly&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T16:09:11-07:00","id":1125724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1125590#post1125590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The very first thing that the crossover section of the Revised W:tA ST Handbook mentions is the incompatible underlying themes. Mage has humans as the center of the cosmos, and has reality altered by sufficient human belief. Werewolf fundamentally rejects both of these, and whether or not you choose to houserule it, it's a very big difference, and the text also notes that either game is going to suffer for crossing over with the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have the book to check at hand right now, so I can't answer adequately. Even if it is that strict in the book, well, some revised writers hated crossover, big deal, nothing new. The WoD in general has enough crossover material to contradict those. <br /> <br /> Also, mages aren't the center of the universe (in my eyes) in Mage, they are the center of the <i>game</i> and yes, could, theoretically change almost anything. That doesn't mean there isn't an Umbra and spirits and myriad other stuff out there, existing regardless of humanity. But again, I'm a fan of the &quot;the consensus isn't absolute and isn't everything&quot; view.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mage doesn't even usually acknowledge that they're in opposition. Stasis isn't trying to trap Entropy in Mage, in any manner, but you'd see that in Werewolf in much more concrete style, because the spirits cause reality to exist in Werewolf. </div> </div> </div>In my opinion, mages just don't see that, because they don't have the stories of the Garou, or believe in them. Being humans, who could alter reality, they probably just think that all they see from the struggles of the triat in the Umbra is a reflection of the mundane world, like weaver spirits, webs, blights and all that. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't want Mage's thematic elements anywhere near a game i'm playing, no. And your entreaty to consider the potential stories falls flat for me, because I didn't get into Werewolf or Changeling for some nonsense involving space battles around Jupiter, only it's really the spirit world for some reason, and there are orbital prisons that are holding Harry and Hermione captive. Also, the system itself rubs me the wrong way, and not just because of a really weird power curve, but because it irons out all the interesting differences between every approach that exists. While Vampire and Demon have their pitfalls and bizarre crossover rules, trying to convince me that a flamethrower is actually like a fireball spell is not one of them. </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay, so you simply don't like Mage. That's fine, play what you like and be happy! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I like both games and I like crossovers, so that's it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for D&amp;D, I don't care what you put in your pseudo-Tolkienesque Forgotten Realms game. Just make sure to use the 1e DMG Boot Hill conversion for guns; the 5e DMG is out of order in making pistols do damage on par with muskets. Though admittedly archaic, the musket's damaging effect is often compared to a shotgun slug.<br /> <br /> (NB: I just referenced one of the least D&amp;D-like D&amp;D settings a few posts ago, so the fantasy hardliner thing made be chuckle a bit.) </div> </div> </div>Umm, that was just an example how some people who have a very clear and strict opinion about what consists of as &quot;thematically appropriate&quot; for a given game or style or genre could be very riled up even about minor things like rapiers and muskets in a traditional medievalesque fantasy setting...<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T20:05:48-07:00","id":1125769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1125724#post1125724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't have the book to check at hand right now, so I can't answer adequately. Even if it is that strict in the book, well, some revised writers hated crossover, big deal, nothing new. The WoD in general has enough crossover material to contradict those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technical problem interaction on the scale that we usually see written about does not solve the larger-scale matter of incompatible universes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, mages aren't the center of the universe (in my eyes) in Mage, they are the center of the <i>game</i> and yes, could, theoretically change almost anything. That doesn't mean there isn't an Umbra and spirits and myriad other stuff out there, existing regardless of humanity. But again, I'm a fan of the &quot;the consensus isn't absolute and isn't everything&quot; view. </div> </div> </div>But that's not how Mage sees things, which is the rub.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my opinion, mages just don't see that, because they don't have the stories of the Garou, or believe in them. Being humans, who could alter reality, they probably just think that all they see from the struggles of the triat in the Umbra is a reflection of the mundane world, like weaver spirits, webs, blights and all that. </div> </div> </div>How they'd manage to miss that, though, especially for Spirit masters, is a great and grand question for the ages when it comes to wider views of the crossover game in question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, okay, so you simply don't like Mage. That's fine, play what you like and be happy! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I like both games and I like crossovers, so that's it. </div> </div> </div>You say &quot;simply&quot;, but it's obviously an elaborate kind of dislike, given the number of factors playing into it. It's hard to like something that's an epic bait and switch that people keep swinging in your face and proclaiming to be the way that all of the games should be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Umm, that was just an example how some people who have a very clear and strict opinion about what consists of as &quot;thematically appropriate&quot; for a given game or style or genre could be very riled up even about minor things like rapiers and muskets in a traditional medievalesque fantasy setting... </div> </div> </div>An oddly-placed equivalence, if it even is one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T17:46:08-07:00","id":1126901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1125769#post1125769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's not how Mage sees things, which is the rub.</div> </div> </div> </div>But M20 itself speaks to the idea that consensus is not all-powerful. Nearly all Mage games I have been involved in do not put human consensus as the end-all be-all of everything. There are definitely spiritual entities out there that do not rely at all on (or care much about) human belief. Sure, the penumbra is a reflection in many ways of material reality, but that does not mean that human consensus dictates all things spirit-related. A mage character might not see things exactly as a Werewolf does, but the game universe does not objectively indicate that human consensus is everything. Also, I would note that most of the World of Darkness line involves an unreliable narrator as well, so it's hard to rely on any one perspective as the absolute truth. I think I would point to the M20 sidebars on this to note how there is not a canon &quot;human consensus = everything&quot; aspect to the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Mage doesn't even usually acknowledge that they're in opposition. Stasis isn't trying to trap Entropy in Mage, in any manner, but you'd see that in Werewolf in much more concrete style, because the spirits cause reality to exist in Werewolf.</i><br /> </div> </div> </div>Some Spirit Mages likely would acknowledge this. The Technocracy has tried to achieve stasis and has ignored the need for Entropy to complete the cycle of decay/destruction. Although mages use a different set of terms (Entropy, Dynamism, Stasis), knoweldgeable spirit mages likely would not see a conflict with how Werewolves view the interaction between the Wyrm, Wyld, and the Weaver. Technocrats might dismiss this, but that just might be because the Technocrats are wrong!<br /> <br /> At the very least, Tradition Mages see the opposition; they just see it in metaphysical terms instead of explicit spiritual terms. Because many mages tend to view spirits as reflections of humanity (at least the lower end ones), they likely would not be surprised at the strength of the Weaver and its interaction with the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> I just do not see the fundamental incompatibility you insist as being present.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12988-imperator","name":"Imperator","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T18:58:04-07:00","id":1126922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imperator</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But M20 itself speaks to the idea that consensus is not all-powerful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it?. Where. I hope you're not talking about the Earthly Foundations, because that's much more contradictory with Werewolf than humans being reality warpers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are definitely spiritual entities out there that do not rely at all on (or care much about) human belief. Sure, the penumbra is a reflection in many ways of material reality, but that does not mean that human consensus dictates all things spirit-related. </div> </div> </div>Definitelly? . It's <b>Insinuated </b>in a few places here and there (but there's little pressence of this in M20), that some spirits may precede human belief. Uthras, Celestines, The Triat. It's <i>insinuated</i> that they may have preexisted the Consensus, but it's <i>never</i> stated in an univocous way. The proclamations of the contrary are more common, but not necessarily more solid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A mage character might not see things exactly as a Werewolf does, but the game universe does not objectively indicate that human consensus is everything. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. There's doubts and holes about the idea that the Consensus it's everything, Mage leaves nothing for certain and that's how things should be to have a &quot;war over the domain of reality&quot;. Absolute relativism won't cut, thus the setting suspends judgement I'm pretty sure that M20 doesn't speak to the idea that consensus is not all-powerful in anything but uncertain terms, and that there's nothing <i>definitive </i>on that matter. That's the game Mage plays, perhaps the Spheres were created by the OoH, or perhaps they where discovered, or re-discovered...perhaps God exists or perhaps it's a paradigmatical construction, we're not telling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think I would point to the M20 sidebars on this to note how there is not a canon &quot;human consensus = everything&quot; aspect to the setting. </div> </div> </div>These sidebars speak to the idea that supernatrurals come from mythic threads that are memes in the universal subconscious...<br /> <br /> Personally, I preffer to think that there are more in the Threads than belief, that they may represent forces that transcend humanity, and old books (like Sorcerer) cater to that idea much better than M20. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Some Spirit Mages likely would acknowledge this. The Technocracy has tried to achieve stasis and has ignored the need for Entropy to complete the cycle of decay/destruction. Although mages use a different set of terms (Entropy, Dynamism, Stasis), knoweldgeable spirit mages likely would not see a conflict with how Werewolves view the interaction between the Wyrm, Wyld, and the Weaver. Technocrats might dismiss this, but that just might be because the Technocrats are wrong! </div> </div> </div>But that's the conundrum, if they are, then Technocrats are unwittingly aiding an extradimensional bug to destroy the universe. This would imply that technocrats are objectively wrong by their own standards. You're just kicking the ball from werewolf to mage. No Technocracy fan would ever accept that the Technocracy it's objectively wrong in such a blatant way, just see all the controversy with the technephandy.<br /> <br /> The best you can do it's to avoid these issues as long as you can: <i>Even, I, the ST, do not know the answer to these profound questions.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just do not see the fundamental incompatibility you insist as being present. </div> </div> </div>In play, there may be none, but it exists and runs pretty deep. For instance, if you travel a lot trough the Umbra you will have to decide if outer space exists or not, or if it exists for Werewolf and not for Mages (regardless of their Paradigm). The very fact that you absolutely have to make this desition points to a contradiction. Also, you would like to scratch the part of M20 where it's stated that cellphones do not work in mystical Reality Zones because the science that sustains them it's based on the Consensus.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-09-2017, 10:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T21:52:34-07:00","id":1126963,"title":"","content":"This is why I prefer WtA to MtAs, it is straightforward and simple by comparison. Then again, so are CtD, KotE, VtM, and WtO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:44:56-07:00","id":1127111,"title":"","content":"Every time my group tried to play Mage, it sometimes felt more trouble than it was worth to follow all the standard rules.<br /> <br /> If a game feels like nuclear physics, then maybe it's just not that fun of a game.<br /> <br /> Or maybe I'm just dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:13:48-07:00","id":1127132,"title":"","content":"No, I am in agreement, though I feel that the complexity comes from the subjectivity of the system rather than the difficulty of the system. I used to be a great fan of MtAs, but I stopped loving it because I kept on having games where entire sessions involved hours of arguing about the exact effects of the Spheres. The problem with MtAs is not only the system, but the fact that the subjectivity of the system allows the inner munchkin of most players to manifest pretty quickly.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T08:53:33-07:00","id":1127151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I used to be a great fan of MtAs, but I stopped loving it because I kept on having games where entire sessions involved hours of arguing about the exact effects of the Spheres. The problem with MtAs is not only the system, but the fact that the subjectivity of the system allows the inner munchkin of most players to manifest pretty quickly.</div> </div> </div> </div>To enjoy Mage you need to be laid back on this subject...just be sure they're interpreting their character's Paradigm, and let them be.<br /> <br /> Being laid back with the rules also helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T12:20:21-07:00","id":1127238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1116926-least-favorite-splat-and-why?p=1127151#post1127151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To enjoy Mage you need to be laid back on this subject...just be sure they're interpreting their character's Paradigm, and let them be.<br /> <br /> Being laid back with the rules also helps.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm actually agreeing with this. I think the problem Fat Larry mentioned manifests itself not because you need to know nuclear physics to play the game, but because (with a bit of exaggeration) the players (read: well-educated, geeky-minded people) know nuclear physics and tend to bring their knowledges into the game, sometimes forgetting to distinct between what they know and what their character knows. Like, lighting up vampires with clever applications of advanced thermodynamics? Turning the room's floor into a substance which would react agressively with the air? Really? How likely the average mage would know about those in depth?<br /> <br /> And I can't even blame them, really, since having a game with a magic system like Mage, which promises messing with the building blocks of reality on that level <i>will</i> bring that out from science-minded people and if restricted, they'd feel themselves robbed and the game misadvertised.<br /> <br /> At one time, I had to argue about &quot;no, your twelve-year old Orphan character won't change a flaslight's beam into sunlight and burn up a whole Sabbat pack with Forces 2 and I don't care how much do you know about photons and frequencies&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 08-10-2017, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}